TASK 1: Understand the Problem and Identify the Data (K4 – Analyse | 4 Marks) 
The Ksheera Village Milk Producers’ Co-operative collects milk twice daily from roughly 300 farmers (scaling to 
6,000 at block level and 150,000 at district union level). Every collection record must be validated and 
computed accurately to the paisa. 
1. Inputs and Outputs 
• Inputs: farmer_id (unique identifier), litres (milk quantity in litres), fat_pct (fat percentage), snf_pct (Solids
Not-Fat percentage), shift ('Morning' or 'Evening'). 
• Outputs: rate_per_litre (computed rate in Rs based on fat/SNF deviations), amount (delivery payout = 
litres × rate_per_litre), ten_day_total (cumulative 10-day payout per farmer and centre). 
2. Named Constants & Data Types 
• Named Constants (Unchanged during execution): BASE_RATE = 30.00, STANDARD_FAT = 3.5, 
STANDARD_SNF = 8.5, FAT_STEP_VALUE = 0.40, SNF_STEP_VALUE = 0.30, MIN_FAT = 2.0, MAX_FAT = 7.0, 
MIN_SNF = 6.0, MAX_SNF = 10.0. 
• Whole Numbers (int): farmer_id, step counts (fat_steps, snf_steps), delivery counts, paise integers. 
• Fractional / Exact Decimal Numbers (float / Decimal): litres, fat_pct, snf_pct, rate_per_litre, amount, 
ten_day_total. 
• Text (str): farmer_id (if alphanumeric, e.g., 'F001'), farmer_name, shift ('Morning'/'Evening'). 
3. Validation Rules & Assumptions 
• Validation Rules: litres > 0 (reject zero or negative quantities); 2.0 <= fat_pct <= 7.0 (valid bovine milk fat 
limits); 6.0 <= snf_pct <= 10.0 (valid SNF limits); shift must be 'Morning' or 'Evening'. 
• Assumptions: Volume in litres is used directly for pricing; deviations from standard 3.5% fat and 8.5% SNF 
are rounded to the nearest 0.1% step; billing occurs strictly in 10-day cycles (20 shifts). 
4. Alternative Concept & Complexity Analysis 
Alternative: Storing each farmer's entry in three separate scalar variables (litres1, fat1, snf1, litres2, fat2, snf2, 
...) instead of a list of tuples/dictionaries. 
• Scalability & Code Structure: For 300 farmers, 900 distinct variable names must be hardcoded. Loops 
cannot iterate cleanly over independent variable names without unsafe eval()/globals() hacks. At 150,000 
farmers, the code becomes impossible to write or maintain. 
• Time Complexity: O(n) to process n entries in both designs, but separate variables incur high 
manual/dispatch overhead and zero code reuse. 
• Space Complexity: O(n) in both, but 3n separate namespace bindings consume more symbol-table 
overhead than a contiguous list of tuples [(litres, fat, snf), ...]. 
