• Rounding Each Payment vs Rounding Only Total: Banks disburse individual farmer payouts rounded to the 
nearest paisa (Rs 0.01). Summing unrounded sub-paisa payouts and rounding once at the end creates a 
discrepancy between the sum of individual farmer receipts and the total bank transfer batch. Rounding 
each payment to 2 decimal places before summing matches bank settlement rules. 
